SteamARM: MetalFX only for a draw that writes the whole output

Patches 14 and 16 replace an upscale draw with MetalFX's spatial scaler,
which writes every texel of the output and nothing else. Patch 16 takes
Source 2's bilinear upsample by the shape of its shader, and Counter-
Strike 2 draws other things with that shader, blended over the picture:
the screen went black at every kill and stayed so, and with scalers made
again and again for passes of many sizes the game stalled and its memory
grew to 7 GB (the user, 2026-10-04).

A draw is replaced only when it does what MetalFX does: one colour
attachment, all four channels written, no blending or logic op, a scissor
covering the output, no depth or stencil test. And past 12 scalers made,
a size not kept is the game's own pass (logged once). Vulkan tests: the
FSR cases (MetalFX, off, dynamic) pass.
diff -ruN a/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/mtl_metalfx.m b/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/mtl_metalfx.m
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/mtl_metalfx.m	2026-10-04 14:26:39
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/mtl_metalfx.m	2026-10-04 14:26:39
@@ -41,6 +41,20 @@
          return s->scaler;
    }
 
+   /* Made again and again (passes of many sizes taken for an upscale), each
+    * one compiled with its own textures: the game stalled and its memory
+    * grew to 7 GB (the user, Counter-Strike 2, 2026-10-04). Past a few, a
+    * size not kept is the game's own pass. */
+   static unsigned made;
+   if (made >= 3 * MFX_SCALERS) {
+      static bool told;
+      if (!told)
+         fprintf(stderr, "kk: FSR by MetalFX: %u scalers made, no more: the game's own passes from now on\n", made);
+      told = true;
+      return nil;
+   }
+   made++;
+
    MTLFXSpatialScalerDescriptor *desc = [MTLFXSpatialScalerDescriptor new];
    desc.inputWidth = in.width;
    desc.inputHeight = in.height;
